WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
A small wooden box sits on a hinged board.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.640
Slowly, the board tilts.

3
00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.720
Steeper, steeper, and then, at one angle,

4
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.970
the box starts to slide.

5
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.160
Now stack a second, identical
box on top and tilt again.

6
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.310
Will the heavier stack grip
better and need a steeper slope?

7
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.660
Or get pulled harder and slide sooner?

8
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.540
In this mission, you'll
split the weight in two:

9
00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:29.190
m g sine theta acting
along the slope, downwards,

10
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.230
and m g cos theta pushing into it.

11
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.930
You'll see that friction can
grow, but only up to mu R.

12
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.700
And that a box about to slide
is in limiting equilibrium.

13
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.470
Your mission: explain why the
box's weight doesn't matter.
